# Controls what `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the Cloud Build context for the
# builds that submit the repo root (vector-rs preview + vector-rs deploy).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: with no .gcloudignore, gcloud falls back to .gitignore,
# whose `data/` rule strips the baked search index (data/index.duckdb) the
# vector-rs image COPYs — so the production build failed with
# "COPY failed: ... stat data/index.duckdb: file does not exist". This file
# overrides that fallback: exclude only heavy/irrelevant artifacts and KEEP
# data/index.duckdb.
#
# (Does not affect sonar-deploy — that submits the `sonar/` dir, so gcloud looks
# for sonar/.gcloudignore, not this root file.)

# VCS + CI config (not needed in the image build)
.git/
.github/

# Local dev / build artifacts. Never present on CI runners; this guards laptop
# `gcloud builds submit` runs from bloating (or timing out) the context upload.
.venv/
venv/
**/target/
node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log

# Everything under data/ EXCEPT the baked production index the Dockerfile needs.
# data/index.duckdb is deliberately NOT excluded.
data/cloudcrate.duckdb
data/*.bak-*
data/sample_cloudcrate.duckdb
data/projection_anchors.json
data/fma/
data/library/
